\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(ci): restore valid durable execute step\",\"oid\":\"6a0b4102ed0b4cfb1aeb613b2d646ac061b193a4\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-09-01T20:19:41Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-09-01T20:19:41Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(vcs): preserve wasm release build support\",\"oid\":\"22e7c77347de23e8b60a69e00c6af8f124d59317\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-09-01T21:33:54Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-09-01T21:33:54Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Entire-Checkpoint: 01M1FE96B8JSK4YWNJRHREPDV7\",\"messageHeadline\":\"merge: resolve main into durable release execution\",\"oid\":\"ab55d67839b47e30f7c6e0e66b18084a249479cd\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-09-01T21:38:55Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-09-01T21:38:55Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Entire-Checkpoint: 01M1FEJCFPGSQC9DBMJ910VXR0\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(deps): acknowledge test-only Wasmtime advisory\",\"oid\":\"c096075c1482953f224ec0c620d5a94ad8edbce1\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-09-01T22:14:37Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-09-01T22:14:37Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge branch 'main' into codex/release-execution-foundation\",\"oid\":\"a85c0c745b89d237a3e607084a67c950c2250be0\"}],\"headRefOid\":\"a85c0c745b89d237a3e607084a67c950c2250be0\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:15:10Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/33565294281/job/100046979823\",\"name\":\"Code Formatting (Moon & Just)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:14:44Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"Callisto CI & Validation\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:15:23Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/33565294281/job/100046979745\",\"name\":\"Clippy Lints (Moon & Just)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:14:45Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"Callisto CI & Validation\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:20:01Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/33565294281/job/100046979691\",\"name\":\"Test Suite & WASM Check (ubuntu-latest)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:14:44Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"Callisto CI & Validation\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:20:48Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/33565294281/job/100046979752\",\"name\":\"Test Suite & WASM Check (macos-latest)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:14:44Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"Callisto CI & Validation\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:20:13Z\",\"conclusion\":\"FAILURE\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/33565294281/job/100046979770\",\"name\":\"Code Coverage & Test Report\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:14:44Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"Callisto CI & Validation\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:15:29Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/33565294281/job/100046979497\",\"name\":\"Security & Advisory Audit (Moon & Just)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:14:45Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"Callisto CI & Validation\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:20:49Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SKIPPED\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/33565294281/job/100048651904\",\"name\":\"Validate Changesets & Workspace Status\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-01T22:20:49Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"Callisto CI & Validation\"}],\"url\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/39\"}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-29T23:51:14Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-29T23:51:14Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…g gaps\\n\\nResolves the plan-job/execute-job architecture contradiction between\\nSPEC-RELEASE-PLAN-DURABILITY-001 (which previously forbade the split) and\\nSPEC-GITHUB-RELEASE-HARDENING-003 (which requires it) and\\nSPEC-RELEASE-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-002 (whose provenance check depends on it).\\n001 now owns the plan-job/execute-job split as its primary architecture,\\nsince GitHub Environment protection is job-scoped only -- there is no way\\nto gate step-level credential access, so 003's stated purpose is\\nunachievable without it.\\n\\nAdopts PR #36's ProvenancePolicy enforcement-point fix (002) and\\n.claude/specs/INDEX.md establishing accepted specs as top-level normative\\nrequirements, replacing the repo-wide dangling linked_requirement fields\\nwith a uniform status/owner_track/last_verified_revision/depends_on\\nmetadata convention across all six specs.\\n\\nIndependently fixes two defects neither branch had resolved (both flagged\\nby an external review): 001's AC-002/AC-005 stale-plan-validation fallback\\ncould let an apply command silently publish a freshly recomputed,\\nunreviewed plan instead of terminally failing on mismatch; 004's advisory\\naudit record was derived from a separate rustsec fetch disconnected from\\nthe actual cargo-deny invocation, so the recorded database revision could\\nsilently diverge from what was actually audited -- now pinned to one\\nrepository-local checkout that both operations share, verified against a\\nlive cargo-deny run.\\n\\nAlso fixes an internal field-naming contradiction introduced while adding\\nthe metadata convention to SPEC-DOCUMENTATION-AUTHORITY-005: its own\\nself-referential AC-002 had independently invented owner/last_verified/\\nstatus:active before this convention existed, colliding with the\\nowner_track/last_verified_revision/status:proposed fields now applied\\nuniformly.\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M17YYFXHTDMRVG895WV0KAEK\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(spec): reconcile release-trust specs with PR #36, close remainin…\",\"oid\":\"39b250aed4ddd6c5cbf10c3b53c14186e7256246\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T01:13:04Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T01:13:04Z\",\"messageBody\":\"001 was split into three specs per the exit-gate's scope-too-large\\nrecommendation (envelope/digest scheme, CLI command-mode split, GitHub\\ntwo-job topology), fixing 12 blockers in the process -- three of them\\nwere code-fact errors in the original spec (VersionPlan isn't serializable\\nso can't be in the envelope, `callisto publish` has no --plan argument\\ntoday, no plan type has deny_unknown_fields), caught by re-verifying every\\ncitation against the real tree rather than carrying them forward.\\n\\n004 fixed 6 blockers, most critically: AC-003's dependency_path format\\nwas unproducable from the command it named (--prefix none discards all\\ntree structure); the exit-1 findings path would have silently dropped\\nthe audit artifact under GitHub Actions' default skip-on-failure step\\nsemantics; and RUSTSEC-form advisory IDs still had no crate-name\\nresolution path (fixed by adding a required `crate` field).\\n\\n006 fixed 3 blockers, including a case where the instructed fix was\\nitself factually wrong -- AC-003b case 4 was prescribed as \\\"identical\\nto no-lane-active\\\", but the cited code has no roster membership check\\nin PreMode::Pre, so an off-roster package still gets prerelease-tagged.\\nVerified against real code and corrected rather than complied with.\\n\\n005's implementation branch was rebuilt on the actual reconciled base\\n(it had drifted onto a stale pre-reconciliation commit) with all three\\nverify-stage gaps closed: mutation-testing unavailability recorded,\\nthe regression harness wired into the lint-docs Justfile recipe, and\\nthe spec's own enrollment fields completed.\\n\\nCross-references in 002/003 updated to point at the correct 001A/001B/001C\\nsub-spec depending on what they actually consume.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(spec): apply gate-recommended fixes to 001/004/005/006\",\"oid\":\"dfdee5cdb75a6ab365f71b9212fb7245c59b8f64\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T01:53:09Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T01:53:09Z\",\"messageBody\":\"PLAN-DOCUMENTATION-AUTHORITY-005.json is the vector:planner plan@1 artifact\\nthat produced the codex/005-doc-authority-v2 branch's commits -- kept for\\ntraceability alongside the spec it implements.\\n\\nCODEX-HANDOFF-RELEASE-TRUST.md summarizes session state for continuation:\\n005 is one test short of done; 001A/001B/001C/004/006 hit real architecture\\nquestions (a callisto-model/callisto-graph dependency cycle, a DepKind\\nordering ambiguity that would silently break digest reproducibility across\\nbuilds, and a tag-after-interrupted-publish logic bug) rather than spec-\\nwording gaps, and are held pending a foundational architecture spec.\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M185XQPFY2XYSW9G3N682A3R\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(plans): add SPEC-005 implementation plan and Codex handoff notes\",\"oid\":\"090b2c730c8d4610610e78ae4b2f9c8878accddc\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T02:36:25Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T02:36:25Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(spec): define durable release execution foundation\",\"oid\":\"fb42f0312d2b11fee2d559b29915d2bf5b53d957\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T02:44:48Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T02:44:48Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(model): add durable release identity and digests\",\"oid\":\"f3f8f4c3eb01871c0170bd1e836fae50cd375b44\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T16:53:50Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T16:53:50Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Entire-Checkpoint: 01M1CBVNVPXP2K9NG806ACY268\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(model): add durable release intent contract\",\"oid\":\"bc92d1f565d27cc70a7beacfbcbf4d655e712ab1\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T18:45:47Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T18:45:47Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(model): validate durable execution state\",\"oid\":\"450b38f534ec73011f60479459aeae127e354cd3\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T19:00:08Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T19:00:08Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(vcs): observe release Git trust evidence\",\"oid\":\"792e4a22e363330f30f0ef613a592e75d910dbd6\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T19:36:46Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T19:36:46Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(vcs): bind release trust to Gi