{"timestamp":"2026-09-01T22:25:58.589Z","ordinal":8084,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a04adc-934d-7aa3-b352-bdba70d0f67c","turn_id":"01a05f10-4390-7220-8c20-684f83cf240e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-770355e8-0e80-4b64-852e-36a049ef5cbf","process_id":"30037","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rtk actionlint .github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml && rtk just --list && rtk git diff --check && rtk git diff -- justfile .github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml"],"cwd":"file:///private/tmp/callisto-release-execution-foundation","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk actionlint .github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml && rtk just --list && rtk git diff --check && rtk git diff -- justfile .github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"    audit                             # Security advisory & license check via moon / cargo-deny\n    build                             # Build debug workspace binaries via moon\n    build-release                     # Build release CLI binary\n    check-api                         # Verify public Rust API SemVer breaking changes\n    ci                                # Run full local CI verification pipeline via moon and just\n    ci-fast                           # needs to regenerate.\n    clean                             # Clean build targets, Moon task caches, and generated artifacts\n    coverage threshold=\"\"             # with the exact same invocation.\n    coverage-per-crate threshold=\"90\" # CI's own coverage step ran first); does not re-run tests itself.\n    default                           # Use `just ci` explicitly for full CI parity including coverage.\n    doc-check                         # Documentation build check (warnings treated as errors)\n    fmt                               # Format code automatically via moon\n    fmt-check                         # Check code formatting compliance via moon\n    fuzz target=\"parse_package_id\"    # Run structure-aware fuzzing target\n    hooks                             # Install native Git pre-commit and pre-push hooks\n    lint                              # internal job scheduler parallelize across crates instead.\n    lint-affected                     # serialization while still skipping unaffected crates entirely.\n    machete                           # Run unused dependency check via cargo-machete\n    mutants                           # Run mutation testing sweep via cargo-mutants\n    pre-commit                        # Fast pre-commit hook validation (<500ms formatting check)\n    pre-push                          # Pre-push hook validation: formatting check plus clippy on affected projects only\n    test                              # Run unit, integration, doctests, and E2E tests\n    wasm-check                        # time under instrumentation -- pure redundant runtime, not extra coverage.\n\n.github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml |  2 ++\n justfile                          | 16 ++++++++++------\n 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\n\nChanges:\n\n.github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml\n  @@ -91,9 +91,11 @@ jobs:\n  +        if: ${{ always() }}\n           with:\n             name: code-coverage-report\n             path: lcov.info\n  +          if-no-files-found: warn\n   \n     security:\n       name: Security & Advisory Audit (Moon & Just)\n  +2 -0\n\njustfile\n  @@ -92,18 +92,22 @@ wasm-check:\n  -# it (--fail-under-lines). Unset locally (informational only, matching\n  -# ARCHITECTURE.md's \"coverage generation is a CI-only gate\" note); CI calls\n  -# `just coverage 90` -- this is the one command both run, so a CI coverage\n  -# failure always reproduces locally with the exact same invocation.\n  +# it (--fail-under-lines). The human-readable summary is always emitted\n  +# before enforcing the threshold: LCOV output itself contains no aggregate\n  +# percentage, and a failed CI gate must say what developers need to improve.\n  +