{"timestamp":"2026-09-01T22:35:10.039Z","ordinal":8258,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a04adc-934d-7aa3-b352-bdba70d0f67c","turn_id":"01a05f18-d73e-7dd3-85d2-d3a848bd8fd1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_066dfde3c06b8029016a97531c3e3c87d093538911e79473ce","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The detailed report also reveals an architectural testing-policy issue: the global gate is measuring the whole inherited workspace, including long-standing low-coverage command modules, while PR #39 adds several large release modules. A blanket 90% line threshold was enabled without a recorded baseline or a changed-code policy. I’m checking the `main` baseline before deciding the correct enforcement model; I won’t lower it just to make this PR green."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788302108269,"completed_at_ms":1788302110039}}
