{"timestamp":"2026-09-01T22:54:10.629Z","ordinal":8614,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a05f2e-14c0-7573-9f5b-a12b4e501f0e","call_id":"call_mql0EyEWsrvSLj1JhmVdjBGX","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 30.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"17-\n18-# CI variant of `test`: emits Nextest's JUnit report under target/nextest/ci\n19-# for the trusted PR reporter. Keep the everyday local command artifact-free.\n20:test-ci:\n21-    cargo nextest run --workspace --profile ci\n22-    cargo test --doc\n23-\n--\n89-    cargo check -p callisto-moon --target wasm32-wasip1 --features pdk\n90-    cargo rustc -p callisto-moon --lib --target wasm32-wasip1 --features pdk --crate-type cdylib\n91-\n92:# Generate code coverage report via cargo-llvm-cov. `_pdk.rs`-suffixed files\n93-# are excluded: they contain code that only executes inside a real\n94-# wasm32-wasip1 Extism host (see e.g. crates/callisto-moon/src/runner_pdk.rs's\n95-# module doc comment) -- black-box tested via tests/moon_wasm_sandbox.rs, but\n--\n105-# generation is a CI-only gate\" note); CI calls `just coverage 90` -- this is\n106-# the one command both run, so a CI coverage failure always reproduces locally\n107-# with the exact same invocation.\n108:coverage threshold=\"\":\n109-    #!/usr/bin/env bash\n110-    set -euo pipefail\n111-    args=(--all-features --lcov --output-path lcov.info --ignore-filename-regex '_pdk\\.rs$')\n112:    cargo llvm-cov \"${args[@]}\"\n113:    cargo llvm-cov report --summary-only --ignore-filename-regex '_pdk\\.rs$'\n114-    if [[ -n \"{{threshold}}\" ]]; then\n115:      cargo llvm-cov report --summary-only --ignore-filename-regex '_pdk\\.rs$' --fail-under-lines \"{{threshold}}\"\n116-    fi\n117-\n118-# Check per-crate line coverage against a threshold (default 90%). The\n119-# workspace-total --fail-under-lines gate can pass while a small crate is\n120-# far below threshold, since a few large crates dominate the total line\n121-# count -- this catches that case. Requires profile data from a prior\n122:# `cargo llvm-cov` run in this session (e.g. `just coverage` just ran, or\n123-# CI's own coverage step ran first); does not re-run tests itself.\n124:coverage-per-crate threshold=\"90\":\n125-    #!/usr/bin/env bash\n126-    set -euo pipefail\n127:    cargo llvm-cov report --json --summary-only --ignore-filename-regex '_pdk\\.rs$' > /tmp/callisto-cov-summary.json\n128-    report=$(jq -r '\n129-        .data[0].files[]\n130-        | select(.filename | test(\"/crates/\"))\n--\n170-\n171-# Same as `ci`, minus `coverage`. Real CI (callisto-ci.yml) already runs\n172-# coverage as its own parallel job on a separate runner; locally it's a\n173:# third full-workspace recompile under llvm-cov instrumentation tacked onto\n174-# the end of a serial pipeline. Use this for everyday pre-PR checks;\n175-# coverage numbers are a reporting concern, not something every local run\n176-# needs to regenerate.\ninfo: cargo-llvm-cov currently setting cfg(coverage); you can opt-out it by passing --no-cfg-coverage\n   Compiling callisto-model v0.5.0 (/private/tmp/callisto-release-execution-foundation/crates/callisto-model)\n   Compiling callisto-manifests v0.5.0 (/private/tmp/callisto-release-execution-foundation/crates/callisto-manifests)\n   Compiling callisto-vcs v0.5.0 (/private/tmp/callisto-release-execution-foundation/crates/callisto-vcs)\n   Compiling callisto-format v0.5.0 (/private/tmp/callisto-release-execution-foundation/crates/callisto-format)\n   Compiling callisto-changelog v0.5.0 (/private/tmp/callisto-release-execution-foundation/crates/callisto-changelog)\n   Compiling callisto-conventional v0.5.0 (/private/tmp/callisto-release-execution-foundation/crates/callisto-conventional)\n   Compiling callisto-fixtures v0.5.0 (/private/tmp/callisto-release-execution-foundation/crates/callisto-fixtures)\n   Compiling callisto-graph v0.5.0 (/private/tmp/callisto-release-ex